---
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
const levels = [
  {
    t: 'Document review',
    d: 'We examine what a supplier can show on paper: registration, tax details, product registrations and, where available, export records.',
    tells: 'Whether the business is what it says it is.',
  },
  {
    t: 'Remote assessment',
    d: 'Structured calls, video walk-throughs and reference samples, measured against your specification.',
    tells: 'Whether capability and product look consistent with the claims.',
  },
  {
    t: 'Physical verification',
    d: 'A site visit, or inspection and laboratory testing by an independent agency, where you agree to it and its cost.',
    tells: 'What is actually present at the facility or in the lot inspected.',
  },
];
const checks = [
  'Business registration and tax details',
  'Applicable product-specific registrations',
  'Export capability and relevant trade history where available',
  'Facility assessment',
  'Product specifications',
  'Reference samples',
  'Independent inspection and testing where agreed',
];
---
<section class="section" id="verification">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHead index="07" label="Supplier evaluation and quality coordination" title="We tell you what was checked, <em>and how.</em>" wide>
      <p>
        “Verified supplier” can mean anything from a certificate received by email to a day spent in the mill.
        We keep the three levels apart and report which one applies to each supplier.
      </p>
    </SectionHead>

    <ol class="levels" role="list">
      {levels.map((l, i) => (
        <li data-reveal style={`--delay:${0.1 * i}s`}>
          <span class="depth" aria-hidden="true">{Array.from({ length: 3 }, (_, j) => <i class:list={{ on: j <= i }} />)}</span>
          <h3>{l.t}</h3>
          <p class="muted">{l.d}</p>
          <p class="tells"><span>What it tells you</span>{l.tells}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <div class="grid lower">
      <div class="checks" data-reveal>
        <h3>What an evaluation can cover</h3>
        <ul role="list">{checks.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}</ul>
      </div>
      <div class="limits" data-reveal style="--delay:.1s">
        <h3>The limits, stated plainly</h3>
        <p>Supplier verification reduces risk but does not eliminate it.</p>
        <p class="muted">
          Not every supplier we present will have been independently audited, and we will say so. A registration
          or certificate shows that a supplier holds it. It does not prove compliance with every requirement of
          your destination market, which remains a matter for the buyer and its advisers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .levels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem); }
  .levels li { display: grid; gap: var(--s-3); align-content: start; border-top: 1px solid var(--c-ink); padding-top: var(--s-5); }
  .depth { display: flex; gap: 4px; margin-bottom: var(--s-3); }
  .depth i { width: 2rem; height: 4px; background: var(--c-line); }
  .depth i.on { background: var(--c-forest); }
  .tells { font-size: var(--t-sm); margin-top: var(--s-2); }
  .tells span, .lower h3 {
    display: block; font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: var(--t-xs); font-weight: 560; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--c-brass-deep);
    margin-bottom: var(--s-2);
  }
  .lower { margin-top: var(--s-8); row-gap: var(--s-7); }
  .checks { grid-column: 1 / span 6; }
  .checks li { padding-block: var(--s-3); border-top: 1px solid var(--c-line); }
  .checks li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-line); }
  .limits { grid-column: 8 / span 5; display: grid; gap: var(--s-4); align-content: start; }
  .limits p:first-of-type { font-family: var(--f-serif); font-size: var(--t-h3); line-height: 1.2; }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .levels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .checks, .limits { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  }
</style>
